  {
    "id": "draft-ch06-006",
    "verdict": "needs_edit",
    "issues": [
      "Explanation is accurate but thinner than the rest of the set and does not reinforce the legal-responsibility point made in the correct option ('follow laws and systems of responsibility'). Expand it so the learner sees why 'publish anything' is wrong."
    ],
    "suggestedExplanationEn": "Swedish media enjoy strong constitutional freedoms under the Freedom of the Press Act (Tryckfrihetsförordningen) and the Fundamental Law on Freedom of Expression (Yttrandefrihetsgrundlagen), but these are not unlimited. Media must still follow laws such as those on defamation, secrecy, and the rules of the responsible publisher (ansvarig utgivare). So 'media may publish anything' is incorrect: broad freedom comes with legal responsibility."
  },
